From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hwsim: reactivate clients present in live snapshots

The hwsim association reconciler made OneWifi's event-backed client map
inactive when the HAL omitted an old or idle station from a live provider
snapshot.  The reverse transition was missing: when traffic made a still
associated station visible to the HAL again, the monitor cache became active
but the event-backed map stayed inactive forever.  Full EasyMesh snapshots
therefore continued to omit a physically associated and reachable client.

Treat a station present in a successful live provider response as current
evidence, restore cli_Active, and publish the same authoritative full update
used for withdrawals.  This makes reconciliation symmetric while retaining
the hwsim-only stale-row filter.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 source/apps/em/wifi_em.c | 16 ++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c b/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c
--- a/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c
+++ b/source/apps/em/wifi_em.c
@@ -666,16 +666,24 @@ static void em_reconcile_live_assoc_snapshot(wifi_mgr_t *wifi_mgr,
     }
     entry = hash_map_get_first(vap->associated_devices_map);
     while (entry != NULL) {
-        if (entry->dev_stats.cli_Active &&
-            !em_live_snapshot_contains(response,
-                entry->dev_stats.cli_MACAddress)) {
-            mac_addr_str_t mac_str;
+        mac_addr_str_t mac_str;
+        bool present = em_live_snapshot_contains(response,
+            entry->dev_stats.cli_MACAddress);
+
+        if (entry->dev_stats.cli_Active && !present) {
             entry->dev_stats.cli_Active = false;
             changed = true;
             to_mac_str(entry->dev_stats.cli_MACAddress, mac_str);
             wifi_util_info_print(WIFI_EM,
                 "%s:%d: live snapshot withdrew stale client %s from vap %u\n",
                 __func__, __LINE__, mac_str, vap_index);
+        } else if (!entry->dev_stats.cli_Active && present) {
+            entry->dev_stats.cli_Active = true;
+            changed = true;
+            to_mac_str(entry->dev_stats.cli_MACAddress, mac_str);
+            wifi_util_info_print(WIFI_EM,
+                "%s:%d: live snapshot restored associated client %s on vap %u\n",
+                __func__, __LINE__, mac_str, vap_index);
         }
         entry = hash_map_get_next(vap->associated_devices_map, entry);
     }
